= Brixton

Over a weekend in April, Brixton burns. Young black men, harassed for months under a police stop-and-search operation called Swamp 81, fight running battles with the police. Hundreds are injured, and buildings and cars are set alight.

- @inquiry: Appoint Lord Scarman to hold an inquiry.
- @crackdown: Back the police, and condemn the rioters without qualification.

@inquiry
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 3; c1_con += 1*(1-dissent); right_dissent += 2

Lord Scarman will report on the causes of the disorder. The right grumbles that excuses are being made for criminals.

@crackdown
on-arrival: right_dissent -= 4; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); c1_lib += 1; de_lab += 1; wet_dissent += 3

"Nothing, but nothing, justifies what happened." The police get new riot equipment.

@toxteth
